# Plugin architecture

## Entry

Default export is a `Plugin` factory:

```ts
const plugin: Plugin = (app) => {
	configureFieldValueResolver(app);
	return {
		name: 'Twitch',
		icon: 'ri:twitch-fill',
		api: publicApi,
		settings: { /* … */ },
		triggers: [/* nested groups */],
		handlers: [/* nested groups */]
	};
};

export default plugin;
```

## Cross-plugin access

Expose typed helpers in `lib/plugin-api.ts` — do not reach into another plugin’s internals:

```ts
export function getTwitch(app: PluginAppApi): TwitchPluginApi {
	return app.plugins.get<TwitchPluginApi>('twitch');
}

export function tryGetTwitch(app: PluginAppApi): TwitchPluginApi | undefined {
	return app.plugins.tryGet<TwitchPluginApi>('twitch');
}
```

## Layout

| Path | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `src/index.ts` | Plugin factory + registration |
| `src/handler/`, `src/trigger/` | Definitions by category |
| `src/lib/` | Domain logic, helpers, `plugin-api.ts` |
| `src/app/` / `widgets/` | Plugin UI |
| `PluginStore` | Persist JSON plugin data |

Use `app.fs` for logs/assets when needed. Keep domain logic out of Svelte components.

## Build

Use shared `plugins/create-vite-build-config.js`. Host modules (`@stream-kit/plugin`, `@stream-kit/core`, `svelte`, `@stream-kit/ui`, …) are **externalized** via `isPluginHostExternal` — never bundle them into the plugin dist.

## Runtime

Plugin UI mounts in a **separate Svelte runtime** (plugin-host). See `plugin-host-runtime.mdc` before debugging or changing plugin UI / shared host modules.
